
  Welcome to MachOS!
  A small operating system with a kernel and userland written in mach.

  To install MachOS on your disk:
    Run `ls -l /dev` to find your disk, then `install /dev/sdX`.
    For an NVMe disk, use `install /dev/nvme0n1`.
    Choose the whole disk, not a partition. Installation erases that disk.

  Getting started:
    `ls /bin` lists commands; `ls --help` explains listing options.
    `config --help` shows how to change persistent system settings.
    `nano FILE` edits text; `less FILE` reads it; `shutdown` powers off.
    `passwd` changes your password; `adduser NAME` creates another account.
    `adduser --admin NAME` creates an administrator; use `se COMMAND`.
    `mpm refresh` refreshes the signed repository; `mpm upgrade` updates the system.

  Arrows recall commands; Tab completes names; Alt+F1..F6 switch terminals.
  Shift+PgUp/PgDn scroll back. First login requires setting a password.

